  "slug": "machine-prediction-fde3",
  "summary": "Preprints now couple protein language models, 3D structure and conformal uncertainty to predict PTM sites, kcat, ADMET and docking error.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is supervised prediction of molecular and residue-level properties from sequence, structure and learned representations, applied to protein function, enzyme kinetics, peptide pharmacokinetics and ligand binding. HieraPTM and SCOPE combine sequence, evolutionary or language-model features with 3D structural context to localize functional sites, with SCOPE reporting mutagenesis validation. EnzRef addresses kcat by modeling reactants and products separately against a frozen protein language model, while AIO targets ADMET of cyclic peptides and macrocycles with segment-level attribution for interpretability. BrainRoute pairs BBB permeability prediction (external balanced accuracy 0.659) with community verification, and the conformal framework quantifies 3D docking uncertainty with dependence-aware intervals. The new element is the emphasis on calibrated uncertainty and interpretability layered onto these predictors.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-24"
}
